# Line-ending policy for cccenter
# ================================
# This repo gets edited from two places that disagree about line endings:
#   - Windows, via C:\DOH\cccenter (writes CRLF)
#   - GitHub's web editor           (writes LF)
#
# Without a policy, every round trip between them rewrites every line of the
# file. Git then reports the whole file as changed, so a one-line edit shows up
# as an 872-line diff and real changes become impossible to spot in a review.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` says: treat files as text, store them as LF in the repo,
# AND check them out as LF in the working tree. Forcing both sides to LF means
# no conversion ever happens, so no phantom diffs. Every editor involved here
# (VS Code, Notepad++, browsers, Python) handles LF without complaint.
#
# Note: plain Windows Notepad on older builds renders LF-only files as one long
# line. Use anything else and it's a non-issue.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending processed — doing so corrupts them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf  binary
